### Rationale
E3 refutes the H16 cap. With the harness flush, a reads-only stream of W takes 45.9 µs with plain loads and 38.7–40 µs with `evict_first`. A real kernel built on that (B ≤ 16) runs at 41.6 and 43.6 µs. The M and L bands use the cuBLASLt TF32 + bias + scatter path from H11, which was not part of E3. The kernel passes 16/16 workloads on the rented B200, with predicted portal score 0.546 (r0: 0.235). I did not record max |err| vs fp64 per B, which the TF32 margin constraint asks for. That check is still open.

